What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/adios_version
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/batch_actual_max
Date:		October 2026
Description:	ADIOS version and maximum observed batch sizes, respectively.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/global_latency_window
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/lat_model_latency_limit
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/lat_target_{read,write,discard}
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Latency window, maximum model sample and per-operation targets,
		respectively, in nanoseconds.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/batch_limit_{read,write,discard}
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/bq_refill_below_ratio
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/batch_order
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/read_priority
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Per-operation batch limits, refill percentage, batch order,
		and read priority. Batch order 0 groups by operation; order 1
		uses sector ordering on rotational devices.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/lat_model_{read,write,discard}
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Latency model base in nanoseconds and slope in nanoseconds per
		KiB. Write two space-separated integers to set the model.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/shrink_at_kreqs
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/shrink_at_gbytes
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/shrink_resist
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/compliance_flags
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Latency-model shrink thresholds and resistance, and compliance
		flags. Bit 0 of compliance_flags disables predicted-latency
		deadline reordering.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/reset_bq_stats
What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iosched/reset_lat_model
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Write 1 to reset batch statistics or latency models. The latter
		also accepts six space-separated base and slope values for the
		read, write, and discard models.
